# The assignment brief itself. It is interface.ai's document, not ours, and this
# repository is public — republishing somebody else's take-home prompt is their
# call to make, not mine. Kept locally; referenced in README and REPORT instead.
Assignment A — Computer-Use Automation System.pdf

# Evidence from demo runs. Following the README's demo path writes 24 run
# directories, which turns `git status` into noise for anybody trying it. The
# curated runs that evidence/README.md explains are already tracked, and git
# never ignores a tracked file, so this only silences new ones. To keep a new
# run as evidence, add it deliberately: `git add -f evidence/<run-id>`.
evidence/*
!evidence/README.md

